                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "10bd632f-f3b9-388e-9c71-e1957d107015",
                        "entry_id": "c201c585-da80-3c5b-a974-90caa7b71b24",
                        "glosses": [
                            "провинция на юге центральной части КНР"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3553ea7c-ab27-4c75-8bcc-ad9eae7144ca",
                                "sense_id": "10bd632f-f3b9-388e-9c71-e1957d107015",
                                "text": "Повидавшись с ним, я узнал, что он отправляется прямо на юг в провинцию Сычуань на границе Тибета, где и поселится на долгое время для этнографических наблюдений, тогда как мне предстояло ехать на запад, чтобы лето посвятить изучению горной страны Наньшань."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d61f0326-7f97-41b5-ace6-637ed0c981a0",
                                "sense_id": "10bd632f-f3b9-388e-9c71-e1957d107015",
                                "text": "Его убили в Сычуани, на пути в Чунцин."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "57a04e82-6a8b-4c43-8d68-7a553b85499a",
                        "source_entry_id": "c201c585-da80-3c5b-a974-90caa7b71b24",
                        "source_sense_id": "10bd632f-f3b9-388e-9c71-e1957d107015",
                        "target_lang_word": "Sichuan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sichuan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1faf3ec-ed7a-312c-889a-748eeab9764f",
                                        "entry_id": "58a5bb9a-fc91-39b5-bd52-a6170706d5a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A province in central China. Capital: Chengdu."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf3c41f6-7715-4952-a236-4a481698c39d",
                                                "sense_id": "b1faf3ec-ed7a-312c-889a-748eeab9764f",
                                                "text": "In Suchue, on Mount Tiexe, the ſtones that grow there being burnt in the fire, drop Iron, which is very fit for the making Swords."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcb929fa-fdfd-459f-af45-870f252a36f0",
                                                "sense_id": "b1faf3ec-ed7a-312c-889a-748eeab9764f",
                                                "text": "SUchuen, which ſignifies Four Waters, is a great Countrey, ſeparated by the River Kiang, into a Northern and Southern part ; Bordering in the Eaſt upon Huquang ; in the South-Eaſt upon Queicheu ; and hath in the North-Eaſt and North Xenſi ; in the North-Weſt, the People Koningguangi and Kiang ; or the Countreys which Paulus Venetus makes to be Preſter John's, which the Chineſes by one general Name call'd Sifan ; and in the Weſt, Tibet, and the moſt Southern part of the Province of Junnan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8d3e4d0-14bd-4b56-8f42-e6cba3a7dc31",
                                                "sense_id": "b1faf3ec-ed7a-312c-889a-748eeab9764f",
                                                "text": "Such was the argument of three highly placed gentlemen of Hubei, graduates of the Japanese military academy and losers in Hubei’s internal conflicts who appeared in Changsha in early 1921. It was also the argument of Xiong Ke-wu, a former military governor of Sichuan whose June visit was concealed behind layers of lies and half truths (he said he was in Changsha to study self-government; gossips in the know said that he was secretly a spokesman for Wang Zhan-yuan)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc54edca-e963-45f4-b788-a5366fda4b04",
                                                "sense_id": "b1faf3ec-ed7a-312c-889a-748eeab9764f",
                                                "text": "China’s agriculture ministry said on Wednesday two new African swine fever outbreaks were confirmed in Sichuan and Qinghai provinces.\nThe new case in the city of Bazhong in Sichuan killed 19 of 117 pigs present on a farm, the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs said in a statement on its website."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00304146-0c54-4093-8ec8-7c38ec896af6",
                                                "sense_id": "b1faf3ec-ed7a-312c-889a-748eeab9764f",
                                                "text": "About 80 percent of wild giant pandas live in Sichuan province. The rest are in Gansu and Shaanxi."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ba94b6bd-1805-4a63-93e5-f0d1d2a6ff93",
